# Chroma library, modern Earth: AIM MOMENTS, group B (aims of knowing and mastering: U, U B and U R), aims v1 (10-19).
# Syntax: header of build.py. Build: python3 build.py earth_aim_moments. Check: python3 tests/check_aims.py . --part
# Every moment is a life event with the five single ways and one full cross cycle. Nothing reads this file until
# the Engine's aims switch is on, so no life changes.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- to know one thing better than anyone (U, cycle s1)

== the question nobody at the library could answer
tier: life event
aim: to know one thing better than anyone
aim_role: spark
stages: juvenile young_adult adult mature elder
age: 12-85
per_year: 0 .5 .4 .4 .3 .3
tone: joy
life: learning, interests
horizon: months
roles: mentor, grandparent, friend, rival
earth: a question about one odd subject that the library has no book to answer
tribal: a question about the river stones that no elder of the clan has ever asked
magic: a question about one corner of the tower's archive that the shelves no longer answer
scene: {N} has a question about one small, odd subject, and the library has run out of books that answer it. The librarian shrugs, and {mentor} wonders aloud who might know.
scene W: {N} wants to do this properly: every source noted, every claim checked against another.
scene U: {N} has filled a notebook already, and the gaps in it are the only interesting part.
scene B: Nobody in town knows more about it than {N} now, and {N} would like that to stay true.
scene R: {N} stayed up until three following one footnote to the next, and is not tired at all.
scene G: {grandparent} knew a little about this once, the old way, and {N} wants to know what they knew.
scene tribal: The elders shrug at {Ns} question about the river stones. Nobody has asked it before, and the only way to know is to watch them for a whole season.
scene magic: The tower's archive holds three shelves on {Ns} odd subject, and {N} has read them all. The keeper says the rest is locked away, or lost.
- W | follow the reading list of the society that studies it, to the letter | v: conformity, achievement | foot: lesson method beats luck | chance: 75
- U | go out and look for the answer yourself, noting every try | v: self-direction, achievement | dream: test | foot: mark learned a skill | chance: 60
- B | track down the one expert who might know, and make them take you seriously | v: power, achievement | foot: person mentor | chance: 50
- R | chase the strangest lead wherever it goes, for a whole summer | v: stimulation, self-direction | foot: means time-.06 | chance: 55
- G | sit with {grandparent} and write down everything they remember of it | v: tradition, benevolence | bond: grandparent +.1 | chance: 80
- W>U | enrol in the evening class on it at the college, and do every exercise | v: conformity, self-direction | foot: place learn.higher | chance: 78
- U>B | trade what you know for a look at a private collection | v: achievement, power | foot: person patron | chance: 45
- B>R | bet {rival} you will have the answer by the spring | v: power, stimulation | foot: person rival | chance: 50
- R>G | drag {friend} along on the hunt for the answer, out in the open air | v: stimulation, benevolence | foot: person friend | chance: 70
- G>W | give your notes to the town library, so the next one starts further on | v: benevolence, universalism | foot: place learn.keeping | chance: 85
works: The answer turns up at last, in the place nobody thought to look, and {N} reads it twice to be sure.
works: {N} knows more about it now than anyone in town, and the question has grown three new ones.
fails: The trail goes cold, and every book {N} finds only repeats the last one.
fails: Months of notes come to nothing, and {N} puts the notebook away for a while.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- to master an instrument (U, cycle s2)

== the piece that finally plays itself
tier: life event
aim: to master an instrument
aim_role: spark
stages: child juvenile young_adult adult mature elder
age: 8-85
per_year: .3 .5 .4 .4 .4 .3
tone: mixed
life: music, interests
horizon: months
roles: grandparent, mentor, friend, teacher
earth: one hard piece that has never once been played through without a stumble
tribal: the long song of the bone flute that only the old player could play without a breath out of place
magic: the hard piece the guild of players asks of every candidate, played by heart
scene: There is one piece {N} has never managed to play through, and the evening is quiet, and the instrument is waiting.
scene W: {N} has a practice chart on the wall, and today's box is still empty.
scene U: {N} has worked out that the trouble is two bars in the middle, and only those two.
scene B: The concert is in a month, and {N} wants the solo more than anyone else does.
scene R: {N} would rather play it wrong and loud than right and dull.
scene G: The piece was {grandparent}'s favourite, and {N} wants to play it the way they used to hum it.
scene tribal: The bone flute has one long song the old player could play through without a breath out of place, and {N} has tried it every night since the thaw.
scene magic: The guild's examiners ask for one hard piece by heart, and {N} has a month and a cold practice room in the tower.
- W | practise the hard bars slowly every morning, a little faster each week | habit | v: conformity, achievement | foot: mark learned a skill | chance: 70
- U | take the two bars apart note by note until the hands understand them | v: self-direction, achievement | dream: test | foot: means time-.06 | chance: 62
- B | play it for the teacher who picks the soloists, before anyone else can | v: achievement, power | foot: person teacher | chance: 48
- R | play it straight through tonight, mistakes and all, as loud as it wants | v: stimulation, hedonism | foot: lesson mistakes can sound alive | chance: 58
- G | play it for {grandparent}, slowly, the old way | v: tradition, benevolence | bond: grandparent +.1 | chance: 80
- W>B | enter the town's music competition and play what the judges expect | v: achievement, conformity | foot: place arts.stage | chance: 45
- U>R | take the hard bars to the Saturday jam at the music shop and play around them | v: self-direction, stimulation | dream: test | foot: place arts.song | chance: 60
- B>G | strike a deal with the old player down the street: garden work for lessons | v: power, benevolence | foot: person mentor | chance: 70
- R>W | play it at the school's open evening, in front of everyone | v: stimulation, conformity | foot: mark took a wild risk | chance: 50
- G>U | learn the piece by ear from an old recording, the way the first players did | v: tradition, self-direction | foot: lesson the ear learns first | chance: 66
works: Somewhere in the second week the hard bars stop being hard, and the piece plays itself.
works: {N} plays it through without a stumble, and the room is very quiet afterwards.
fails: The same two bars break down again, and {N} closes the lid harder than meant to.
fails: The piece gets worse before it gets better, and this week it only gets worse.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- to teach well (U, cycle s3)

== the lesson that finally lands
tier: life event
aim: to teach well
aim_role: spark
stages: juvenile young_adult adult mature elder
age: 15-80
per_year: 0 .4 .5 .5 .4 .2
tone: mixed
life: school, work
horizon: week
roles: colleague, mentor, parent, a pupil who has given up
earth: a pupil who has not understood the same thing after three tries
tribal: a young one of the band who cannot learn the knot that holds the snare
magic: a first-year of the academy who cannot hold the simplest figure in mind
scene: {N} has been asked to explain something to a younger pupil who has not understood it in three tries, and the hour is running out.
scene W: {N} follows the method in the textbook, step by careful step.
scene U: {N} keeps wondering where exactly the pupil's picture of it goes wrong.
scene B: {N} would like this pupil's marks to go up, visibly, and soon.
scene R: {N} is bored of the worksheet too, and suspects the pupil can tell.
scene G: {N} remembers being stuck on exactly this, and how it felt.
scene tribal: A young one of the band cannot learn the knot that holds the snare, and has cried over it twice. The elders have left {N} to show it again.
scene magic: A first-year at the academy cannot hold the simplest figure in mind, and the master has handed the pupil to {N} for the afternoon.
- W | go back to the first step and build it up, one rule at a time | v: conformity, benevolence | foot: lesson start from the beginning | chance: 75
- U | ask the pupil to explain it back, and listen for where it breaks | v: self-direction, benevolence | dream: test | foot: mark learned a skill | chance: 65
- B | promise the pupil's parents better marks by the end of term | v: achievement, power | foot: door kept your word | chance: 50
- R | throw away the worksheet and teach it as a game, and let the others join in | v: stimulation, hedonism | foot: means ties+.03 | chance: 60
- G | admit how long it took you, and sit with the pupil till it comes | v: benevolence | foot: means time-.04 | chance: 80
- W>R | start a lively study group for the whole class, every Friday | v: conformity, stimulation | foot: place gather.circle | chance: 70
- U>G | take the lesson outside and show it with sticks and stones on the ground | v: self-direction, universalism | dream: test | foot: mark helped someone in need | chance: 62
- B>W | offer to tutor the pupil after school, for a fair fee | v: achievement, security | foot: means money+.02 | chance: 60
- R>U | make up a silly song that holds the rule, and sing it till it sticks | v: stimulation, self-direction | foot: lesson a joke can carry a rule | chance: 66
- G>B | ask the old teacher who taught you how they would do it | v: tradition, achievement | foot: person mentor | chance: 75
works: Halfway through the fourth try the pupil's face changes, and {N} sees the moment it lands.
works: The pupil gets the next one right alone, and then the one after that.
fails: The pupil nods politely and has clearly understood nothing.
fails: The hour runs out with the pupil more muddled than before, and {N} goes home turning it over.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- to find out what is true (U, cycle s4)

== the argument with the old believer
tier: life event
aim: to find out what is true
aim_role: spark
stages: juvenile young_adult adult mature elder
age: 13-90
per_year: 0 .4 .4 .4 .4 .3
tone: mixed
life: faith, meaning
horizon: months
roles: elder, friend, mentor, parent
earth: a long evening with an old believer, and a question that will not be left alone
tribal: the old telling of how the first people came out of the river, and a river that ends in marsh
magic: an old servant of the temple, and a scroll in the archive that tells the story differently
scene: {N} has spent a long evening with {elder}, who has believed the same thing all their life, and {N} has a question that will not be left alone.
scene W: {N} wants to be fair to both sides, and to the old ways.
scene U: {N} has read three books that disagree, and wants to know which one is true.
scene B: {N} suspects most people believe what is useful to them, and wonders what is useful to {elder}.
scene R: {N} feels something huge just behind the words, and wants to feel it properly.
scene G: {elder} raised half the street in this faith, and {N} does not want to break anything.
scene tribal: Around the fire {elder} tells again how the first people came out of the river. {N} has walked the river to its end and found only marsh.
scene magic: {elder} has served the temple of the old powers for fifty years. {N} has found a scroll in the archive that tells the story differently.
- W | hear {elder} out to the end before saying a word | v: tradition, benevolence | bond: elder +.1 | chance: 85
- U | ask {elder} the hard question plainly, and weigh the answer honestly | v: self-direction, universalism | dream: test | foot: person mentor | chance: 55
- B | win the argument point by point, whatever it costs | v: power, achievement | break: elder | chance: 60
- R | go to the service with {elder}, and see what it feels like from inside | v: stimulation, self-direction | foot: place faith.congregation | chance: 70
- G | let it lie, and keep the peace at the table | v: tradition, security | dream: drop | foot: lesson some questions can wait | chance: 85
- W>G | join the circle where believers and doubters talk once a month | v: universalism, benevolence | foot: place gather.talk | chance: 75
- U>W | read the holy book from the first page to the last, with notes | v: self-direction, conformity | dream: test | foot: place learn.keeping | chance: 65
- B>U | put to the clergy the questions you know they cannot answer | v: power, self-direction | foot: mark defied an authority | chance: 50
- R>B | go off alone to the retreat in the hills to find out for yourself | v: stimulation, self-direction | foot: place faith.seeking | chance: 60
- G>R | walk the old pilgrim path with {elder}, and argue the whole way | v: tradition, stimulation | foot: place faith.shrines | chance: 70
works: {N} comes away without a final answer but with a truer question, and {elder} looks almost pleased.
works: Something in {Ns} thinking settles, and the next morning the world looks slightly different.
fails: The evening ends in a silence neither of them knows how to break.
fails: Every answer {N} finds only leads to two more, and none of them feels like the truth.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- to be the best at what I do (U B, cycle s1)

== the job only the best could finish
tier: life event
aim: to be the best at what I do
aim_role: spark
stages: young_adult adult mature
age: 17-70
needs: career
per_year: 0 0 .4 .4 .3 0
tone: mixed
life: work
horizon: months
roles: boss, colleague, rival, mentor
earth: a job two others have already given up on, left on one desk
tribal: the old hunter's great spear-thrower, cracked, that two carvers have failed to mend
magic: a commission for a great house that a master of the guild has failed to finish
scene: A job has come in that two others have already given up on, and {boss} has put it on {Ns} desk with a look that says: if anyone can.
scene W: {N} intends to do it by the book, every check signed off.
scene U: {N} has already spotted why the others failed, and it is almost beautiful.
scene B: Whoever finishes this will be talked about, and {N} means to be the one.
scene R: {N} has never wanted a job so badly, and has never been so unsure of finishing it.
scene G: The job is for a small firm that has been with the company for thirty years, and {N} knows the family.
scene tribal: The old hunter's great spear-thrower has cracked, and two carvers have failed to mend it. {elder} hands it to {N} without a word.
scene magic: A master of the guild has failed at a commission for a great house, and the guild gives it to {N} with a month to finish.
- W | work through it step by step, checking each part against the standard | v: conformity, achievement | foot: lesson the standard has its reasons | chance: 60
- U | find the flaw the others missed and solve it from the root | v: achievement, self-direction | dream: test | foot: mark learned a skill | chance: 50
- B | take the job and the credit, and let nobody else near it | v: power, achievement | dream: test | foot: person colleague lost | chance: 52
- R | stay late every night until it is done | v: stimulation, achievement | foot: means health-.05 | chance: 55
- G | ring the family the job is for, and ask what they really need | v: benevolence, security | foot: means ties+.04 | chance: 80
- W>U | ask for the proper training course before touching it | v: conformity, self-direction | foot: place learn.higher | chance: 75
- U>B | solve it quietly, then name your price for the next one | v: achievement, power | foot: means money+.06 | chance: 50
- B>R | bet {rival} in the next office that you will crack it by Friday | v: power, stimulation | foot: person rival | chance: 50
- R>G | bring {colleague} in on it, and make it fun | v: stimulation, benevolence | foot: person friend | chance: 68
- G>W | turn it down, and say plainly that it needs a specialist | v: security, benevolence | dream: drop | foot: door turned down a chance | chance: 90
works: It takes longer than anyone hoped, but it works, and {boss} stops by twice to look at it.
works: Word goes round the floor that {N} finished what nobody else could.
fails: The job beats {N} too, and goes back on the pile with a third name on it.
fails: It almost works, and almost is what everyone remembers.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- to marry well (U B, cycle s2)

== the dinner with the family who matters
tier: life event
aim: to marry well
aim_role: spark
stages: young_adult adult
age: 18-50
per_year: 0 0 .4 .3 0 0
tone: mixed
life: love, family
horizon: week
roles: prospect, parent, friend, elder
earth: Sunday dinner with the family of someone worth marrying: the big house, the old name, the questions
tribal: a meal at the fire of a strong clan, whose mother has asked to see the one her child favours
magic: a dinner at an old house of the city, with the steward watching every move
scene: {prospect} has asked {N} to Sunday dinner with the family: the big house, the old name, and an uncle who asks about prospects.
scene W: {N} has brought flowers, a gift for the hosts, and the best manners {N} owns.
scene U: {N} has quietly worked out who in the family decides things, and it is not the one doing the talking.
scene B: The family has a firm, land and a name, and {N} can see the life that comes with them.
scene R: {N} cannot stop looking at {prospect}, and the family is a blur.
scene G: {N} is watching how the family treat each other, and whether there is room at the table for one more.
scene tribal: {prospect}'s clan holds the best grounds by the river, and the mother of the clan has asked {N} to eat at her fire.
scene magic: {prospect} is of an old house of the city, and the house has asked {N} to dine, with the steward watching every move.
- W | thank the hosts properly and mind every manner | v: conformity, tradition | foot: lesson manners open doors | chance: 80
- U | listen more than talk, and learn how this family really works | v: self-direction, security | dream: test | bond: prospect +.1 | chance: 70
- B | let the uncle know exactly what you bring to the match | v: power, achievement | dream: test | foot: person patron | chance: 50
- R | forget the family and spend the evening making {prospect} laugh | v: hedonism, stimulation | foot: lesson love does not do sums | chance: 75
- G | help the grandmother clear the table, and hear the family's stories | v: benevolence, tradition | foot: person elder | chance: 85
- W>B | ask the family's leave to court {prospect}, as the old families expect | v: tradition, power | foot: door kept your word | chance: 55
- U>R | debate the uncle across the table, and enjoy every minute | v: self-direction, stimulation | foot: person rival | chance: 55
- B>G | offer to help out in the family firm, and see where it leads | v: power, security | foot: place comm.shop | chance: 60
- R>W | propose to {prospect} on the walk home, ring or no ring | v: stimulation, conformity | title: engaged | chance: 40
- G>U | decide on the way home that a good match is not enough, and say so kindly | v: benevolence, self-direction | dream: drop | break: prospect | chance: 85
works: The head of the family walks {N} to the door and lingers over the goodbye.
works: On the way home {prospect} says the family liked {N}, and sounds surprised.
fails: The uncle's questions get sharper with every course, and {N} leaves with a headache.
fails: The family is polite all evening, and that is all it is.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- to keep a sharp eye on money (U B, cycle s3)

== the accounts that do not add up
tier: life event
aim: to keep a sharp eye on money
aim_role: spark
stages: juvenile young_adult adult mature elder
age: 14-80
per_year: 0 .3 .5 .5 .4 .2
tone: trouble
life: money, work
horizon: week
roles: boss, colleague, friend, parent
earth: the books of the club, the shop or the family firm, with a gap nobody can explain
tribal: the clan's winter stores, fewer baskets than the tally sticks say
magic: the vault-book of a merchant house that does not match the coin in the vault
scene: {N} has been handed the books of the club, or the shop, or the family firm, and there is a gap in them that nobody can explain.
scene W: {N} wants every figure right, and right in writing.
scene U: {N} has the columns spread across the table and a feeling the answer is in the dates.
scene B: Someone has been careless, or clever, and {N} wants to know which, and what it is worth.
scene R: {N} is itching to rip the whole system up and start again.
scene G: The firm feeds three families, and {N} keeps thinking of them while turning the pages.
scene tribal: The clan's winter stores were counted at the first frost, and now there are fewer baskets than the tally sticks say. The elders want {N} to find out why.
scene magic: The vault-book of the merchant house does not match the coin in the vault, and the steward has given {N} three days to find the missing sum.
- W | go through every line twice, and report exactly what you find | v: conformity, security | foot: lesson write everything down | chance: 70
- U | trace the gap back through the dates until the pattern shows | v: self-direction, achievement | dream: test | foot: mark learned a skill | chance: 60
- B | find the gap, and keep quiet about it until it is useful | v: power, security | dream: test | foot: door kept it hidden | chance: 55
- R | throw out the old ledgers and set up a new system from scratch | v: stimulation, self-direction | foot: means time-.06 | chance: 50
- G | ask the old bookkeeper over a cup of tea how it used to be done | v: tradition, benevolence | foot: person mentor | chance: 80
- W>R | call a meeting of the committee and lay the whole thing on the table, loudly | v: conformity, stimulation | foot: place rule.counsel | chance: 55
- U>G | build a simple sheet so that anyone in the family can follow the money | v: self-direction, benevolence | foot: means ties+.04 | chance: 75
- B>W | offer to keep the books properly from now on, for a fee | v: power, security | foot: means money+.05 | chance: 65
- R>U | sign up for the night course in accounts on a whim | v: stimulation, self-direction | foot: place learn.higher | chance: 75
- G>B | quietly cover the gap from your own savings, to spare the family | v: benevolence, security | foot: means money-.06 | chance: 85
works: The gap closes at last: a payment made twice, three years back, and {N} can prove it.
works: The books balance to the last coin, and {N} sleeps well for the first time in a week.
fails: The figures refuse to meet, and the gap is still there at the end of the month.
fails: {N} finds the mistake, and makes a new one fixing it.

