scene tribal: The oldest telling of the first people has words in it that nobody alive understands. {elder} says the meaning went with the last old singer.
scene magic: The temple's first scroll is in a tongue only three scholars in the realm can read, and one of them has just agreed to see {N}.
- W | take the page to the minister and ask for the accepted reading | v: tradition, conformity | foot: place faith.congregation | chance: 80
- U | learn the old tongue word by word until the page reads itself | v: self-direction, achievement | dream: test | foot: mark learned a skill | chance: 50
- B | find the one scholar who reads it, and make yourself useful to them | v: power, achievement | dream: test | foot: person mentor | chance: 55
- R | read the page aloud over and over until it means something | v: stimulation, self-direction | foot: lesson words carry more than meaning | chance: 60
- G | ask {grandparent} how the old words sounded at home | v: tradition, benevolence | bond: grandparent +.1 | chance: 85
- W>G | join the study group that meets in the old chapel on Thursdays | v: conformity, benevolence | foot: place gather.talk | chance: 78
