works: One word at a time the page opens, and what it says is stranger and kinder than the translation.
works: {N} reads the first line in the old tongue unaided, and has to sit down.
fails: The old words stay shut, and the dictionary only argues with itself.
fails: Every reading {N} tries falls apart at the same word.

